# dnstt tunnel configs
# One dns:// URI per line. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# Format: dns://BASE64(JSON)
# The JSON contains:
#   ps       - config name (for display/scoring)
#   ns       - NS domain (e.g., d1.yourdomain.com)
#   pubkey   - server's dnstt public key (hex)
#   addr     - resolver address (IP for UDP, URL for DoH)
#   transport - "udp" or "doh"
#
# Example (UDP via Cloudflare resolver):
# dns://eyJwcyI6Im15LWNmLXVkcCIsIm5zIjoiZDEueW91cmRvbWFpbi5jb20iLCJwdWJrZXkiOiJhYmNkZWYxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwiYWRkciI6IjEuMS4xLjEiLCJ0cmFuc3BvcnQiOiJ1ZHAifQ==
#
# Example (DoH via Google):
# dns://eyJwcyI6Im15LWdnLWRvaCIsIm5zIjoiZDEueW91cmRvbWFpbi5jb20iLCJwdWJrZXkiOiJhYmNkZWYxMjM0NTY3ODkwIiwiYWRkciI6Imh0dHBzOi8vOC44LjguOC9kbnMtcXVlcnkiLCJ0cmFuc3BvcnQiOiJkb2gifQ==
#
# To generate configs, use the generate_configs.py script or create them manually:
#   1. Set up dnstt-server on your VPS (see server/dnstt/)
#   2. Note the public key from server/dnstt/keys/server.pub
#   3. Create DNS records: A record for ns1.yourdomain.com -> server IP (DNS only!)
#                          NS record for d1.yourdomain.com -> ns1.yourdomain.com
#   4. Base64-encode the JSON and prefix with dns://
